  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={n\\in N:|\\frac{n}{4}|=3}?$",
  "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the natural numbers that satisfy the equation $|\\frac{n}{4}|=3.$ So, we first need to solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{n}{4}| & =3 \\\\ \\frac{n}{4} & =\\pm 3 \\\\ n & =\\pm 12 \\\\ n & =-12,12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $n=-12$ and $n=12.$ However, since $-12\\notin N,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains only one element, namely $n=12.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the given set as\n\n$$\nA={12}.\n$$",
